    "tenYearAvg": 115761519,
    "note": "Spider-Man: Brand New Day held #1 for a second-straight weekend, dropping 60% to an estimated $145M and pushing its 10-day domestic cume past $655M (worldwide north of $930M). That's the third-best domestic second weekend of all time, trailing only The Force Awakens ($149.2M) and Avengers: Endgame ($147.4M), and clearing Avengers: Infinity War's $114.8M third-place mark. The Odyssey slipped 38% to $31.5M in its fourth weekend, crossing $461M domestic and roughly $910M worldwide. Two new wide entries underwhelmed: Universal's One Night Only opened to an estimated $5.7M (3,012 theaters) and Searchlight's Super Troopers 3 debuted to $4.0M (2,760 theaters), both landing below their long-range Box Office Pro calls. With holdovers Toy Story 5, Minions & Monsters and Moana continuing to fade, the overall market is estimated at $205M-$210M for the frame — a steep comedown from the record $436M+ notched the prior weekend, but still running well ahead of both last year's comparable weekend ($131.2M) and the 10-year average for the slot ($115.8M)."
  },
