  "projections": [
    {
      "title": "The End of Oak Street",
      "distributor": "Warner Bros.",
      "theaters": 3400,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "momentum": "rising",
      "rtCritic": null,
      "metacritic": null,
      "rangeLow": 25000000,
      "rangeHigh": 45000000,
      "analysis": "The Quorum's tracking has swung hard in Oak Street's favor over the past month. Awareness climbed +14 and interest +8 across three straight reads, reversing an earlier slide and positioning it as one of two films (alongside Aug. 21's Insidious: Out of the Further) battling to be August's surprise breakout. Forecasts have widened as a result: Box Office Pro's original $25M–$35M long-range call has given way to a broader $25M–$45M spread elsewhere, with most predictions clustering in the low $30Ms. Comps run the gamut — Warner Bros.' original-IP high-water mark is Sinners' $48M open, while genre disappointments like Trap ($15.4M), Mickey 17 ($19M) and The Creator ($14M) mark the floor. Director David Robert Mitchell hasn't had a wide release since 2014's It Follows — an 11-year gap that tempers the Weapons ($43.5M open) comparison somewhat. Running in roughly 3,400 theaters, opposite PAW Patrol: The Dino Movie the same weekend.",
      "rulerLow": 20000000,
      "rulerHigh": 48000000,
      "currentEstimate": null,
      "estimateColorMode": "gradient",
      "estimateColor": "#5C8FF0"
    },
    {
      "title": "PAW Patrol: The Dino Movie",
      "distributor": "Paramount",
      "theaters": 3200,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "momentum": "stable",
      "rtCritic": null,
      "metacritic": null,
      "rangeLow": 15000000,
      "rangeHigh": 20000000,
      "analysis": "Long-range calls from Box Office Pro ($15M–$20M) and other trackers (Deadline/Forbes converge around $14M–$19M) have held steady since forecasting began in late July, with roughly 3,200 theaters expected. Franchise history sets modest expectations: 2021's Paw Patrol: The Movie opened to $13.1M en route to a $40.1M domestic total, while 2023's Paw Patrol: The Mighty Movie bowed to $22.7M in September. Recent August/September family comps include The Wild Robot ($35.7M), The Bad Guys 2 ($21.9M) and Gabby's Dollhouse: The Movie ($13.6M). Going head-to-head the same day against Warner Bros.' The End of Oak Street — both effectively dinosaur movies — outlets are framing Aug. 14 as a family-vs-genre 'dino box office battle,' though PAW Patrol's built-in preschool audience should largely insulate it from direct competition with Oak Street's older-skewing pitch.",
      "rulerLow": 12000000,
      "rulerHigh": 22000000,
      "currentEstimate": null,
      "estimateColorMode": "gradient",
      "estimateColor": "#5C8FF0"
    },
    {
